  "documentation": {
    "content": "1. Check if there are any failed disks : storage disk show -broken\n2. Make sure the failed drive is not in the same RAID group as the missing disk: aggro show-status -aggregate !aggr0*\n\nIf they both are on the same RAID group, the risk of losing data is high, contact support with a P0.\n\nIf there are no failed disks and the cluster has only one missing drive, then open a case to support with cluster serial number and error message. In almost all the cases, the resolution would be to replace the drive.\n\n${metric_or_resource.labels}",
